# Coring Module Design

The `coring` module defines the core domain classes: the data structures that
represent layouts, topics, events, and tasks as read from the YAML configuration.

`coring` classes are **plain data holders** — they store parsed values and expose
typed getters/setters. They do not resolve cross-entity references (e.g. a topic's
`parent_ids` stays as a `list[str]`), do not apply inheritance, and contain no
scheduling logic. That responsibility belongs to `backending`.

Imports allowed: `utilizing` only.

---

## File map

```
src/yasched/coring/
  _shared.py        # small support types shared by multiple classes
  Layout.py         # Layout + BackgroundStyle + BorderStyle + IconStyle
  Schedule.py       # abstract Schedule base
  WeeklySchedule.py
  MonthlySchedule.py
  YearlySchedule.py
  SingleDaySchedule.py
  MultiDaySchedule.py
  Topic.py
  Event.py
  Task.py
```

---

## _shared.py — Support types

Small types that do not warrant their own file, shared across two or more classes.

### Weekday (enum)

Days of the week. Used by `WeeklySchedule` and `WeeklyAppointment`.

```python
class Weekday(enum.Enum):
    MONDAY = "monday"
    TUESDAY = "tuesday"
    WEDNESDAY = "wednesday"
    THURSDAY = "thursday"
    FRIDAY = "friday"
    SATURDAY = "saturday"
    SUNDAY = "sunday"
```

### WeeklyAppointment

One time slot within a weekly recurring schedule.
Exactly one of `end_time` or `duration` must be set.

| Field        | Type               | Required | Description                        |
|--------------|--------------------|----------|------------------------------------|
| `week_day`   | `Weekday`          | yes      | Day of the week                    |
| `start_time` | `datetime.time`    | yes      | Start time                         |
| `end_time`   | `datetime.time`    | no       | End time (mutually exclusive with `duration`) |
| `duration`   | `Duration`         | no       | Duration (mutually exclusive with `end_time`) |

### TaskStatus (enum)

```python
class TaskStatus(enum.Enum):
    TODO       = "todo"
    IN_PROGRESS = "in_progress"
    DONE       = "done"
    CANCELLED  = "cancelled"
    BLOCKED    = "blocked"
```

Default when omitted in YAML: `TODO`.

### EffortRange

Estimated effort bounds for a task. Both fields use `Duration`.

| Field | Type       | Required | Description         |
|-------|------------|----------|---------------------|
| `min` | `Duration` | yes      | Minimum estimate    |
| `max` | `Duration` | yes      | Maximum estimate    |

Invariant: `min.total_minutes <= max.total_minutes`.

### EventLink

A reference from a task to an event, with behavioral flags.

| Field              | Type   | Default | Description                                          |
|--------------------|--------|---------|------------------------------------------------------|
| `event_id`         | `str`  | —       | ID of the linked event                               |
| `use_as_deadline`  | `bool` | `True`  | Sync the task's deadline to the event's date         |
| `as_context`       | `bool` | `True`  | Show this task alongside the event in views          |

YAML shorthand `events: [math_exam]` expands to `EventLink(event_id="math_exam")` with both flags `True`.

### BlockedBy

A dependency that prevents a task from starting.

| Field         | Type          | Required | Description                             |
|---------------|---------------|----------|-----------------------------------------|
| `task_id`     | `str`         | yes      | ID of the blocking task                 |
| `description` | `str \| None` | no       | Human-readable reason for the block     |

---

## Layout

**File:** `src/yasched/coring/Layout.py`

Visual style applied to topics, events, or tasks. Can be defined inline or
referenced by id (a bare string pointing to a predefined layout).

Contains three optional sub-objects. All sub-classes live in the same file
since they have no independent identity.

### BackgroundStyle

| Field    | Type                   | Description                                          |
|----------|------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| `type`   | `str`                  | `"solid"` or `"gradient"`                            |
| `color`  | `Color \| None`        | Single color (for solid)                             |
| `colors` | `list[Color] \| None`  | Color stops (for gradient)                           |

### BorderStyle

| Field   | Type          | Description                     |
|---------|---------------|---------------------------------|
| `type`  | `str`         | `"solid"` (only value so far)   |
| `width` | `str`         | CSS-style width, e.g. `"2px"`   |
| `color` | `Color`       | Border color                    |

### IconStyle

| Field   | Type  | Description                          |
|---------|-------|--------------------------------------|
| `type`  | `str` | `"emoji"` or `"image"`               |
| `value` | `str` | Emoji character or image path/URL    |

### Layout

| Field        | Type                      | Description                    |
|--------------|---------------------------|--------------------------------|
| `id`         | `str \| None`             | Set when the layout is named   |
| `background` | `BackgroundStyle \| None` |                                |
| `border`     | `BorderStyle \| None`     |                                |
| `icon`       | `IconStyle \| None`       |                                |

The `layout` field on `Topic`, `Event`, and `Task` is typed as `Layout | str`:
- `str` → unresolved reference to a named layout id (resolved by `backending`)
- `Layout` → inline definition

---

## Schedule hierarchy

**Files:** `src/yasched/coring/Schedule.py` (abstract base) + one file per subclass.

Used by both `Event.schedules` and `Task.schedules` (recurring tasks).
All schedules are stored as a `list[Schedule]` — single-schedule entities use
a one-element list.

### Schedule (abstract base)

```
Schedule [abstract]
```

No shared fields; the abstract class only provides the common type.

### WeeklySchedule

Repeats on specified days of the week.
Appointments can be expressed as a uniform pattern (`week_days` + shared
`start_time`/`duration`) or as explicit per-day appointments.

| Field          | Type                       | Required | Description                                    |
|----------------|----------------------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|
| `appointments` | `list[WeeklyAppointment]`  | yes      | One entry per day/time slot                    |
| `start_date`   | `datetime.date \| None`    | no       | First occurrence date (inclusive)              |
| `end_date`     | `datetime.date \| None`    | no       | Last occurrence date (inclusive)               |

YAML shorthand `week_days: [monday, wednesday] / start_time: 10:00 / duration: 1h`
expands to one `WeeklyAppointment` per listed day with the shared time/duration.

### MonthlySchedule

Repeats on a fixed day of the month.

| Field          | Type            | Required | Description                     |
|----------------|-----------------|----------|---------------------------------|
| `day_of_month` | `int`           | yes      | 1–28 (cap at 28 for safety)     |
| `start_time`   | `datetime.time` | yes      |                                 |
| `duration`     | `Duration`      | yes      |                                 |
| `start_date`   | `datetime.date \| None` | no |                               |
| `end_date`     | `datetime.date \| None` | no |                               |

### YearlySchedule

Repeats once per year on a fixed month and day.

| Field   | Type  | Required | Description                     |
|---------|-------|----------|---------------------------------|
| `month` | `int` | yes      | 1–12                            |
| `day`   | `int` | yes      | 1–31 (validated per month)      |

### SingleDaySchedule

A one-off occurrence on a specific calendar date.

| Field        | Type                    | Required | Description                               |
|--------------|-------------------------|----------|-------------------------------------------|
| `day`        | `datetime.date`         | yes      | The date of the occurrence               |
| `start_time` | `datetime.time \| None` | no       | Start time (all-day event if omitted)    |
| `duration`   | `Duration \| None`      | no       | Duration (open-ended if omitted)         |

### MultiDaySchedule

A one-off occurrence spanning multiple calendar days (all-day range).

| Field       | Type            | Required | Description                     |
|-------------|-----------------|----------|---------------------------------|
| `start_day` | `datetime.date` | yes      | First day (inclusive)           |
| `end_day`   | `datetime.date` | yes      | Last day (inclusive)            |

Invariant: `start_day <= end_day`.

---

## Topic

**File:** `src/yasched/coring/Topic.py`

Organizational category. Topics form a DAG via `parent_ids`. Tags and layout
are inherited from parents — resolution happens in `backending`.

| Field        | Type               | Required | Description                                     |
|--------------|--------------------|----------|-------------------------------------------------|
| `id`         | `str`              | yes      | Unique identifier                               |
| `name`       | `str`              | yes      | Human-readable display name                     |
| `description`| `str \| None`      | no       |                                                 |
| `tags`       | `list[str]`        | no       | Empty list if omitted                           |
| `parent_ids` | `list[str]`        | no       | IDs of parent topics (unresolved references)    |
| `layout`     | `Layout \| str \| None` | no  | Inline layout or reference to a named layout id |

---

## Event

**File:** `src/yasched/coring/Event.py`

A time-bound occurrence. May recur. Optionally flags overlapping events.

| Field            | Type                    | Required | Description                                             |
|------------------|-------------------------|----------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| `id`             | `str`                   | yes      |                                                         |
| `topic_id`       | `str`                   | yes      | ID of the owning topic                                  |
| `name`           | `str`                   | yes      |                                                         |
| `description`    | `str \| None`           | no       |                                                         |
| `location`       | `str \| None`           | no       | Free text: room name, address, or URL                   |
| `schedules`      | `list[Schedule]`        | yes      | At least one schedule entry                             |
| `layout`         | `Layout \| str \| None` | no       | Overrides topic layout if set                           |
| `blocking_level` | `int \| None`           | no       | Flags overlapping events with level ≤ this value        |

### blocking_level semantics

When an event has `blocking_level: N`, any other event whose schedule overlaps
in time and whose own `blocking_level` is ≤ N is shown with a visual warning.
Events with no `blocking_level` are treated as level 0 and are always flagged
by a blocking event. Tasks are not affected.

---

## Task

**File:** `src/yasched/coring/Task.py`

A unit of work. May be a one-off with a deadline, a recurring task (via
`schedules`), or a subtask of another task (via `parent_id`).

| Field          | Type                    | Required | Description                                                    |
|----------------|-------------------------|----------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| `id`           | `str`                   | yes      |                                                                |
| `topic_id`     | `str \| None`           | no       | Inherited from `parent_id`'s topic if omitted                  |
| `parent_id`    | `str \| None`           | no       | ID of the parent task (for subtasks)                           |
| `name`         | `str`                   | yes      |                                                                |
| `description`  | `str \| None`           | no       |                                                                |
| `tags`         | `list[str]`             | no       | Overrides parent/topic tags when set                           |
| `deadline`     | `datetime.date \| None` | no       | Hard deadline; may be synced from a linked event               |
| `priority`     | `int \| None`           | no       | 1 = lowest; higher = more urgent; no upper bound               |
| `status`       | `TaskStatus`            | no       | Default: `TaskStatus.TODO`                                     |
| `effort`       | `EffortRange \| None`   | no       | Estimated effort bounds                                        |
| `schedules`    | `list[Schedule]`        | no       | Non-empty only for recurring tasks                             |
| `event_links`  | `list[EventLink]`       | no       | Links to related events                                        |
| `blocked_by`   | `list[BlockedBy]`       | no       | Tasks that must complete before this one can start             |
| `layout`       | `Layout \| str \| None` | no       | Overrides parent/topic layout if set                           |

### Invariants

- A task with `schedules` must not also have a `deadline` (the schedule defines timing).
- A task with `parent_id` inherits `topic_id`, `tags`, and `layout` from the parent
  unless those fields are explicitly set. Resolution is done by `backending`.
- `status: BLOCKED` is an explicit override; `blocked_by` entries drive the same
  semantic but the status must be set manually — they are not automatically synced.

